# ShowSouk — local environment.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored and must stay that way: this
# repo is public, and the file was tracked until 2026-08-28. It only ever held
# the publishable values below — which ship in the browser bundle anyway, so
# nothing was leaked — but the pattern is what matters. A service-role key or an
# ingest token landing in that file would have been published.
#
# Production does not read this file. Vercel holds its own copy of every value,
# including the two secrets at the bottom that are deliberately absent here.

# --- Client, safe to expose -------------------------------------------------
# These are compiled into the browser bundle by Vite, so they are public by
# design. The publishable (anon) key is constrained by row-level security.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://<project-ref>.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="<publishable-anon-key>"
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="<project-ref>"

# Server-side aliases of the same three, read by the API route handlers when
# import.meta.env is not available.
SUPABASE_URL="https://<project-ref>.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="<publishable-anon-key>"
SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="<project-ref>"

# --- Secrets — set in Vercel, NOT here --------------------------------------
# Listed so you know they exist and what breaks without them. Both live in the
# Vercel project's environment variables and are intentionally unavailable on a
# dev machine, which is why the scraper cannot be run locally against live data
# (see §11.25 of CLAUDE-HANDOVER.md).
#
#   SCRAPER_INGEST_TOKEN   authenticates the SECURITY DEFINER write functions
#                          (ingest_cinema_films, set_posters, touch_films,
#                          page_cache_*). Without it the scrape routes return
#                          500 rather than writing anything.
#
#   TMDB_API_KEY           poster and backdrop resolution. Accepts either a v3
#                          API key or a v4 read-access token. Without it
#                          resolve-posters exits cleanly and artwork stays
#                          hotlinked — an upgrade path, never a hard dependency.
